      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Shebang and Variables",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Shebang and Running",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Shebang is ==line 1 only==; the kernel reads it on exec",
                "`#!/usr/bin/env bash` picks bash from ==PATH==",
                "`#!/bin/bash` is a fixed path"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Run",
                "Shebang",
                "Runs in",
                "Vars persist"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`chmod +x s.sh && ./s.sh`",
                  "used",
                  "child",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`bash s.sh`",
                  "ignored",
                  "child",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`source s.sh`",
                  "ignored",
                  "{green:current shell}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Variables",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "name=world          # no spaces around =",
                "greet=${name:-hi}   # fallback if unset or empty",
                "now=$(date +%F)     # command substitution",
                "n=$((n+1))          # arithmetic",
                "readonly MAX=3",
                "export MODE=dev"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`readonly` blocks reassignment; `export` shows it to child processes",
                "Untyped strings; ==global== unless `local` in a function"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why env bash?** It finds bash on PATH, so it works where bash is not in /bin",
                "**./s.sh vs source?** `./` runs a child shell; `source` runs in the current one",
                "**Why does `x = 5` fail?** The spaces make `x` a command with two arguments"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Quoting and Expansion Rules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Quoting and Expansion Rules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Quotes and Splitting",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Unquoted `$var` is ==word-split== and glob-expanded",
                "`f='my file.txt'`; `rm $f` gets {red:two args}",
                "Always write ==\"$var\"==",
                "`\"...\"` keeps `$var`, `$(cmd)`; `\\` escapes only `$` backtick `\"` `\\`",
                "`'...'` is fully {blue:literal}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Prints"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`echo \"$HOME\"`",
                  "the path"
                ],
                [
                  "`echo '$HOME'`",
                  "`$HOME`"
                ],
                [
                  "`\"a\\nb\"`",
                  "stays literal"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Forwarding Arguments",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Expands to"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`\"$@\"`",
                  "each arg as a ==separate word==: forward with this"
                ],
                [
                  "`\"$*\"`",
                  "all args joined into {red:one string}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Tests",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`[[ ]]`: left side needs no quotes; `==` is ==pattern match==",
                "`[ ]`: unquoted empty var gives a {red:syntax error}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**`rm $dir/*` with a space or empty `$dir`?** Splits into extra args; empty becomes `rm /*`",
                "**Single vs double quotes?** Single is literal; double expands `$` and `$(cmd)`",
                "**`\"$@\"` vs `\"$*\"`?** Separate words vs one string"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Quote every ==$var==; forward arguments with `\"$@\"`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Conditionals and Loops",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Conditionals and Loops",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Tests Run Commands",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`if cmd; then ...; elif ...; else ...; fi` tests ==exit status==",
                "{green:0 = true}, {red:nonzero = false}",
                "`[ ]` and `[[ ]]` are just commands returning a status"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "`[ ]`",
                "`[[ ]]`"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Origin",
                  "POSIX",
                  "bash-native"
                ],
                [
                  "Quoting",
                  "needed",
                  "no splitting"
                ],
                [
                  "And / or",
                  "`-a` `-o`",
                  "`&&` `||`"
                ],
                [
                  "Regex",
                  "no",
                  "`=~`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Common Tests",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`-f` file, `-d` dir, `-e` exists",
                "`-z` empty string, `-n` non-empty",
                "`-eq -lt -gt` integers; `==` strings"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Loops",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "for f in *.log; do echo \"$f\"; done",
                "for ((i=0;i<5;i++)); do echo \"$i\"; done",
                "while read -r line; do echo \"$line\"; done < file",
                "until cmd; do sleep 1; done"
              ],
              "note": "break leaves the loop, continue skips to the next pass"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**`[ ]` vs `[[ ]]`?** POSIX command vs bash keyword: no splitting, `&&`, `=~`",
                "**Why `while read -r`?** `for` over `$(cat f)` splits on spaces; `-r` keeps backslashes",
                "**`if grep -q x f` tests?** grep's exit status: 0 when a match is found"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Functions, Arguments and Exit Status",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Functions, Arguments and Exit Status",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Functions and Arguments",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Define `name() { ...; }`, call it like a command",
                "Inside: `$1 $2 ...` and `$#`",
                "`local x=1` keeps ==x== out of the global scope"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Item",
                "Means"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`$0`",
                  "script name"
                ],
                [
                  "`$1`..`$9`",
                  "positional"
                ],
                [
                  "`${10}`",
                  "needs braces"
                ],
                [
                  "`$#` / `$@`",
                  "count / all args"
                ],
                [
                  "`shift`",
                  "drops `$1`"
                ],
                [
                  "`${1:-fallback}`",
                  "default if unset"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Exit Status",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`return n` and `exit n` set a status ==0-255==",
                "`return` leaves the function; `exit` ends the script",
                "`$?` = last status, ==overwritten== by the next command",
                "`exit 0` = success, anything else = {red:failure}",
                "Functions return a status; data goes out via stdout: `result=$(fn)`",
                "Test success with `if fn; then`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "greet() { echo \"hi $1\"; }",
                "msg=$(greet bob)",
                "check() { [[ -f \"$1\" ]]; }",
                "if check /etc/passwd; then echo ok; fi",
                "echo \"$msg\""
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "ok",
                "hi bob"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**String back?** `echo` it, capture with `$(fn)`",
                "**`$?`** last status, reset by every command",
                "**return vs exit** function vs whole script"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Strict Mode and Cron",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Strict Mode and Cron",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Strict mode",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`set -e`",
                  "exit on first failing command"
                ],
                [
                  "`set -u`",
                  "unset variable is an error"
                ],
                [
                  "`set -o pipefail`",
                  "pipeline fails if any stage fails"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Put ==set -euo pipefail== at the top of the script",
                "`set -e` skips `if`/`while` conditions",
                "Also skips any `&&`/`||` command except the last: `false && x` lives, `true && false` exits",
                "Without pipefail, `false | true` returns 0 and hides the failure"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "false | true; echo $?",
                "set -o pipefail",
                "false | true; echo $?"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "0",
                "1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cron",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fields: `min hour dom mon dow command`",
                "`crontab -e` edits, `crontab -l` lists"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Schedule",
                "Runs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`*/5 * * * *`",
                  "every 5 minutes"
                ],
                [
                  "`0 2 * * 1`",
                  "02:00 on Mondays"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Works in terminal, fails in cron",
              "text": "Cron has a minimal PATH and no login environment. Use absolute paths, set `PATH=` at the top, and add `>> /var/log/job.log 2>&1` or output mail is lost."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
